Provenance
----------
Portions of the Cognito custom authentication trigger logic (the
Define/Create/Verify auth challenge handlers) are derived from the AWS sample
"cognito-custom-authentication" (email MFA backend), originally published under
the MIT-0 (MIT No Attribution) license by Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.
The derived code has been adapted to replace the emailed one-time code with a
World ID Live Check: CreateAuthChallenge signs a Relying-Party request (via a
Node signer that reads the signing key from AWS Secrets Manager),
VerifyAuthChallengeResponse forwards the returned proof to the World ID verify
API. Using World ID 4.0 session proofs, the first sign-in binds a World ID
session to the Cognito account, and later sign-ins must prove that session.

